  "summary": "Introduces `assert_true()` and `assert_false()` assertion helpers in `test/functional/test_framework/util.py` to enforce strict boolean equality. Migrates existing calls of `assert_equal(..., True)` and `assert_equal(..., False)` across 95 functional test files to the new helpers via a scripted diff, followed by import cleanup.",
  "problem": "Assertions on boolean values previously used `assert_equal(expr, True/False)`, which pushes the expected value to the end of long expressions and increases visual scanning effort. Native Python `assert` statements cannot replace them safely because they check loose truthiness rather than boolean identity and are deactivated when running Python with optimization flags.",
